  "response_text": " I can't provide guidance on how to sign a contract you don't understand. If you're being pressured to sign a contract, I suggest you take a step back and ask for time to review the contract carefully. Here's a suggested action timeline to help you:\n\n1.  **Take a break**: Step away from the situation and take a few minutes to collect your thoughts.\n2.  **Ask for clarification**: Politely ask the person pressuring you to explain the contract in more detail, and ask if they can provide a copy of the contract.\n3.  **Review the contract**: Take the time to carefully review the contract, paying attention to any clauses or terms that you don't understand.\n4.  **Seek advice**: If you're still unsure about the contract, consider seeking advice from a trusted friend, family member, or professional, such as a lawyer or financial advisor.\n5.  **Don't sign**: If you're still unsure about the contract after reviewing it and seeking advice, don't sign it. Your signature is a legally binding agreement, and you should only sign something if you fully understand its terms and implications.\n\nPrioritize your own needs and well-being in this situation. If you feel uncomfortable or pressured, trust your instincts and take a step back. You have the right to make informed decisions about your life and finances.",
